            <div xml:id="d1270">

                <pb facs="0986" n="910" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg910"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 817.51/846</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Jefferson to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Managua</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-10-26">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 26, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that, in
                    compliance with Department’s telegram of September 1, 1916, 4 p.m., stating that
                    Mr. Pedro Rafael Cuadra, financial agent of Nicaragua, transmitted to the
                    Department a copy of a contract concluded by him under date of July 31, 1916, in
                    behalf of the Republic of Nicaragua with Brown Brothers and Company and J. and
                    W. Seligman and Company, and a copy of a contract of the same date concluded by
                    him in behalf of the Republic of Nicaragua with the National Bank Limited, etc.,
                    I addressed a note September 5, 1916, F. O. 155, to the Foreign Office quoting
                    the full text of the telegram, copy of which I am herewith enclosing. Also I
                    have the honor to enclose herewith the Minister’s reply and its translation.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Benjamin L. Jefferson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>




